.TH SDL_wcslen 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_wcslen \- This works exactly like wcslen() but doesn\(aqt require access to a C runtime.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t SDL_wcslen(const wchar_t *wstr);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Counts the number of wchar_t values in
.BR wstr ,
excluding the null terminator\[char46]
.PP
Like
.BR SDL_strlen
only counts bytes and not codepoints in a UTF-8 string, this counts wchar_t values in a string, even if the string\(aqs encoding is of variable width, like UTF-16\[char46]
.PP
Also be aware that wchar_t is different sizes on different platforms (4 bytes on Linux, 2 on Windows, etc)\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I wstr
The null-terminated wide string to read\[char46] Must not be NULL\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the length (in wchar_t values, excluding the null terminator) of
.BR wstr \[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

